WEBVTT

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:10.590
<b><i>Summer vacation is half over, and we're just past the hump.</i></b>

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:16.760
<b><i>Starting today, the Yumegaoka High School 
Diving Club is holding its summer training camp!</i></b>

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.320
<b>All right Teko, let's begin your navigation lesson.</b>

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:20.950
<b>Okay!</b>

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.150
<b>First, hold your compass level with the ground.</b>

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.540
<b>Level with the ground.</b>

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.840
<b>Point the lubber line straight at me. {## 'straight between' is just not correct for reasons, and 'align' sort of does want to take a -line- here and not just a direction, so that's why 'point'}</b>

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.510
<b>Done!</b>

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.760
<b>Rotate the bezel until the index marks match up with north. {## there's two 'marks', or we consider them a single 'marker', but it's certainly not a single 'mark'}</b>

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.430
<b>Got it?</b>

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.930
<b>Yes!</b>

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.140
<b>Now take ten steps towards me.</b>

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.570
<b>You can take your time. Just make sure the marks don't stray from north. {## 'north arrow' implies other directional arrows but anyway it's just not necessary. it's the index mark what's straying because the arrow always points north. minor, but}</b>

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:48.900
<b>Okay.</b>

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.860
<b>One. Two.</b>

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.820
<b>Three. Four.</b>

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.280
<b>Five. Six. Seven.</b>

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.750
<b>Eight. Nine. Ten!</b>

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Okay, good.</b>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.210
<b>Now return to where you started. {## it's more natural, and successive orders like this is fine}</b>

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.740
<b>Rotate the bezel 180 degrees.</b>

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.580
<b>Then turn your body until north 
lines up with the index marks again. {## oh, so -this- is why. I don't care, though. if you really want you can have 'arrow pointing north' or something}</b>

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:22.100
<b>Take ten more paces with the same stride, 
making sure you keep it between the marks.</b>

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.770
<b>One. Two.</b>

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:29.650
<b>Three. Four.</b>

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.530
<b>Five. Six.</b>

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:36.990
<b>Seven. Eight. Nine.</b>

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:38.450
<b>Ten.</b>

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.510
<b>Right on the mark, Teko!</b>

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:42.990
<b>Just look behind you!</b>

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.120
<b>I came back exactly the way I went!</b>

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.990
<b>I was only looking at my compass the whole time, too.</b>

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.760
<b>When underwater, there are times you can barely see even three meters ahead.</b>

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.580
<b>Knowing how to use a compass is invaluable to keeping track of your location.{## '[verb phrase] is [adj] for [noun]' just a bit awkward in engl}</b>

00:01:58.580 --> 00:01:59.470
<b>Right!</b>

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:03.710
<b>All right, let's hop into the sea and put our lesson into practice. {## 'it' ends up half referring to 'the sea' and parallel blah blah}</b>

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:04.750
<b>Okay!</b>

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.270
<b><i>Doing it for real in the sea.</i></b>

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.720
<b><i>Yeah, I've got this. I can do it!</i></b>

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.210
<b><i>...I hope. {this is like the onlyu time I'll use leading ellipses like this}{## you used the old version of the OP lyrics, you}</i></b>

